{
  "//": [
    "THE LATTICE -- roads, rail, towns, yards and garrisons.",
    "",
    "Ported from modelgen/gen_town.py and gen_industry.py. Geometry is data now:",
    "a list of primitives, built by the editor, with no Blender in the loop.",
    "",
    "Conventions: 1 unit = 1 metre, Y up, origin at ground centre. `cell` names",
    "a palette square; row 7 (e_*) is emissive. `bevel` defaults to 0.03 because",
    "the art bible puts a chamfer on every edge -- set it to 0 only for parts",
    "nobody will stand next to. See docs/TOOLING.md for the full primitive list.",
    "",
    "Art rules these were built to: straight lines are the storytelling, because",
    "nothing in nature is straight. Everything is worn -- a pristine road would",
    "read as somebody else's live city rather than a dead one. Ground pieces stay",
    "under 0.5 m so they never block sightlines to machines."
  ],

